  "title": "Local holes do not measure how deep a network's hole is",
  "subject": "The program's plain hole criterion on networks of knots",
  "conclusion": "In the complex of partial solutions, every knot that excludes two or more states is a hole at its own scope, so the plain hole criterion certifies only the trivial level 2 on parity, sum-mod-3 and not-all-equal networks. How far local reasoning must look is set by the whole network's cuts, not by the shape of its knots.",
